Property:

Conductors: Conductivity between

$10^4 – 10^6 \, \Omega^{-1} \, \text{cm}^{-1}$

 

Semiconductors: Materials having electrical conductivity between conductors

$10^{-6} – 10^4 \, \Omega^{-1} \, \text{cm}^{-1}$

and insulators

$10^{-18} – 10^{-8} \, \Omega^{-1} \, \text{cm}^{-1}$
 

They have conductivity between:

$10^{-8} – 10^3 \, \Omega^{-1} \, \text{cm}^{-1}$

Conductivity of a semiconductor can be varied by the process of doping.
Conductivity can also be varied by changes in temperature, optical excitation, and impurity content.